# Gmail

Call the Gmail API as the connected user through the Gmail MCP server
connected to this session. The session's MCP relay attaches the user's
credential on every call; never ask for or handle credentials yourself.

{{ACTION_AVAILABILITY_SECTION}}

## Usage

Read tools (messages, threads, labels, drafts, profile) run freely. The
writes are sending, modifying labels, trashing, and the draft operations;
there is no permanent message delete. `me` is always the connected user.

Prefer drafts when an email needs the user's review: a draft saves an email
without sending it, so the user can check and send it from Gmail.

### List / search messages

Lists message headers (From, Subject, Date, snippet). Search takes Gmail
search syntax (e.g. `is:unread from:boss@x.com newer_than:7d`).

### One message

Full message with its decoded plain-text body.

### Read a thread

A whole conversation, each message with its decoded plain-text body.

