### Drafts

List drafts (each summarised like a message), or read one with its decoded
body.

### Update a draft (write, not sent)

Updating a draft replaces the whole draft.

### Delete / send a draft (write)

Deleting a draft permanently removes it. Sending a draft sends the existing
draft as an email.

### Download an attachment

Attachment ids come from a message's payload parts (fetch the message first);
binary bytes are never printed to stdout — ask for a file output when the
tool offers one.

## Output

Tool results are JSON. List tools return the items and whether more existed
past the limit; failures include Google's error (with `code` and `message`) —
surface the error rather than retrying blindly.

## Notes

- Message bodies are returned decoded from base64url; for multipart messages
  the first `text/plain` part is used.
- Common system label IDs: `INBOX`, `UNREAD`, `STARRED`, `SENT`, `TRASH`,
  `SPAM`, `IMPORTANT`.
